    {
      "id": "daemon-config-validation",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "Daemon construction now validates DaemonConfig against the schema: a missing required field or a value of the wrong JSON type or literal throws DaemonConfigInvalidError (some fields were previously passed through unchecked), and the bin reports every config error at once. DaemonConfigFieldRemovedError gains a required `migration` (constructor third argument) pointing at the removed-field table; a removed field such as workspaceRoot keeps throwing it. Fix the reported fields; a Host that constructs DaemonConfigFieldRemovedError itself passes the migration anchor.",
      "migration": "docs/spec.md#removed-daemonconfig-fields",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#DaemonConfigFieldRemovedError"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "host-layout-helper",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "resolveHostLayout({ productId, productName, platform?, homeDir?, env? }) returns the recommended storeDir (the SDK default ~/.byok/<productId>, with its #493 scratch placement and socket-path budget), hostStorageRoot (macOS ~/Library/Application Support/<productName>, Linux $XDG_DATA_HOME/<productId>, Windows %LOCALAPPDATA%\\<productName>), its agents directory and the service log directory. It is pure and throws HostLayoutInputError (code host_layout_input_invalid, with the field) on an input it cannot lay out. DaemonEffectiveConfig.directories gains logDir. Nothing to change; a Host that computes these directories itself can call the helper instead. Existing stores do not move.",
      "migration": "docs/spec.md#recommended-host-layout",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#HostLayout",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#HostLayoutInputError",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#HostLayoutOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#HostLayoutPlatform",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#resolveHostLayout"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "device-store-default-dir-removed",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "The static DeviceStore.defaultDir(productId) is removed; it duplicated the default store path. The class is reachable through BlobClient and InstallSkillPacksOptions. The default storeDir is still <home>/.byok/<productId> and no store moves. A Host that called DeviceStore.defaultDir uses resolveHostLayout({ productId, productName }).storeDir. These same exports also contain private AuthManager declaration changes for the token-renewal minimum gap (#1114): a fast device clock or short server TTL no longer loops renewals and keychain writes. That renewal fix requires no additional Host action.",
      "migration": "docs/spec.md#recommended-host-layout",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#BlobClient",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#InstallSkillPacksOptions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "capability-ports-two-way",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "createByokCloud now refuses a port passed without its capability declared (capability_port_undeclared), as it already refused a capability declared without its port (#1096). Hosts that pass a port without declaring it must either declare the capability or stop passing the port. createByokServer no longer passes an E2EE member store and derives its declaration from its ports with the new capabilityDeclarationForPorts; createInMemoryByokCloud's default declaration is derived the same way. SqliteSchemaErrorCode drops SQLITE_MIGRATION_REFUSED, which only the removed E2EE KEM-floor check raised.",
      "migration": "docs/architecture/process-namespace-topology.md#capability-ports-migration",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#CLOUD_ERROR_CODES",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#CapabilityPorts",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#capabilityDeclarationForPorts",
        "export:@byok-sdk/server#SqliteSchemaErrorCode"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "store-compatibility-precheck",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "Read-only store compatibility precheck (#1102). Before switching versions, run the candidate build's inspectors to learn whether it accepts each local store, needs a new path and pairing (new-path-repair), or refuses it (rejected): inspectDaemonStores (@byok-sdk/client, journal and pi-durable replicas; also `byok-agent upgrade check --store [--json]`, exit 2 when a store would be refused), inspectSqliteStore (@byok-sdk/server) and inspectProviderProfileStore (@byok-sdk/keys), all returning the StoreCompatibility type from @byok-sdk/core. Each one opens only a private temporary copy of the files.",
      "migration": "docs/upgrade-manifest.md#store-compatibility-precheck",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#InspectDaemonStoresInput",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#inspectDaemonStores",
        "export:@byok-sdk/core#LocalStoreId",
        "export:@byok-sdk/core#StoreCompatibility",
        "export:@byok-sdk/core#StoreCompatibilityVerdict",
        "export:@byok-sdk/keys#inspectProviderProfileStore",
        "export:@byok-sdk/server#inspectSqliteStore"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "task-fail-reason-bound",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "The task.fail reason schema now transforms with boundFailureReason (#1124): createEnvelope and every decode redact credentials (Authorization/Bearer values, provider key shapes, *KEY/*TOKEN/*SECRET/*PASSWORD* assignments, URL userinfo) and cap the reason at TASK_FAIL_REASON_MAX_BYTES UTF-8 bytes with a truncation marker. A longer reason is truncated, never refused, and no field is removed; machine-readable failure stays in task.fail.failure. Breaking because decode no longer returns such a reason verbatim: a Host that parsed the stderr tail out of reason must read the local daemon diagnostics instead, and a terminal receipt stored before this release whose reason is unbounded is not rewritten and no longer re-encodes byte-for-byte, so settle in-flight task terminals before upgrading the cloud.",
      "migration": "docs/security.md#runtime-operation-admission",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#TASK_FAIL_REASON_MAX_BYTES",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#TaskFailPayloadSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#boundFailureReason",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol/constants#TASK_FAIL_REASON_MAX_BYTES",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol/constants#boundFailureReason"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "storage-retention-bounds",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "Every retention class declares a bound (#1105). The SDK now expires Pi's own session files in DaemonConfig.piByokLauncher.sessionDir (class pi-session-dir, 31 days by last write) and -task- terminal evidence in each Agent home (class terminal-evidence, 30 days); both moved from ProtectedClassId to ExpiringClassId, and the never-populated retired-namespace class is gone. New protected class runtime-session-external registers runtime session records outside the Agent home. storage.retention.ttlMs['pi-session-dir'] must be at least ttlMs['session-ledger'] plus one day, else LocalStorageConfigError. A Host that trimmed the Pi session folder itself deletes that code; a Host that raised the session-ledger TTL raises the pi-session-dir TTL too.",
      "migration": "docs/host-local-storage-layout.md#retention-bounds",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#ExpiringClassId",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#ProtectedClassId",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#resolveStorageConfig"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pi-session-retention-lifecycle",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "Prepared operations that own swept session data expose acquireSessionLease. TaskRunner acquires it before validating a resume handoff and passes the exact local RuntimeSessionLease to start; callers retain it until confirmed disposal. Pi admission and actual child writer gates coordinate shared session directories, including parent crashes and native session replacement.",
      "migration": "docs/host-local-storage-layout.md#retention-bounds",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#PreparedRuntimeOperation",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#RuntimeOperationStartInput",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#RuntimeSessionLease",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#PreparedRuntimeOperation",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#RuntimeOperationStartInput",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#RuntimeSessionLease"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auth-revocation-typed-keychain-deadline",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "Renewal halts as revoked at once only on the typed /byok/challenge or /byok/token 401 body {error, code: 'device_not_registered'}, which the reference handlers now send for an unknown or revoked device. Any other 401 backs off, rechecks once, and halts only if the recheck is rejected too. Every OS keychain command has a deadline and is killed on timeout or daemon stop (DeviceCredentialCommandAbortedError); DeviceCredentialBackend methods take an optional AbortSignal that an injected backend should honor (#1117). A custom server without the typed body still halts, after the one recheck.",
      "migration": "docs/protocol.md#63-revocation",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#DeviceCredentialBackend",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#DeviceCredentialCommandAbortedError",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#DEVICE_NOT_REGISTERED_CODE",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#DeviceNotRegisteredResponse",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#DeviceNotRegisteredResponseSchema"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "device-store-pairing-binding",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "A storeDir only uses the OS enrollment its own pair-time device.json names (#1094). Startup, status, identity and the stored signer no longer self-heal a missing or different device.json from the productId-keyed OS entry: they throw DeviceStoreBindingMismatchError (code device_store_not_bound), and start halts as the new DaemonHaltReason 'store_not_bound'. Pairing refuses while the OS entry holds an enrollment this storeDir did not pair, unless Daemon.pair(code, { replaceOtherStore: true }) / byok-agent pair --replace-other-store. Unpair from such a store fails closed.",
      "migration": "docs/device-setup.md#troubleshooting",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#DAEMON_HALT_REASONS",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#Daemon",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#DeviceStoreBindingMismatchError"
      ]
    }
  ],
